  "data": {
    "accession": "PXD032728",
    "title": "Analysis of subcellular Importin b1 interactomes by BioID and BAR proximity labelling",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "Importin 1 (KPNB1) is a nucleocytoplasmic transport factor with critical roles in both cytoplasmic and nucleocytoplasmic transport, hence there is keen interest in the characterization of its subcellular interactomes. We found limited efficiency of BioID in detection of importin complex cargos, and therefore generated a highly specific and sensitive anti-KPNB1 monoclonal antibody to enable Biotinylation by Antibody Recognition (BAR) analysis of Importin 1 interactomes.",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Protein digestion was performed on-beads. Sample-incubated streptavidin magnetic beads were treated with 5 mM DTT in 20 mM ammonium bicarbonate, and alkylation followed with 15 mM iodoacetamide, followed by overnight treatment with trypsin, peptide recovery and desalting using a C18 Zip tip for mass spectrometry analysis",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "Data were searched against the mouse subsets of the SwissProt database (UniProtKB.2013.6.17) (plus the corresponding randomized sequences to calculate FRD on the searches), using Protein Prospector. 1% FDR was allowed on searches for each individual sample, then results were merged.",
